{
  "manufacturer": "MENNEKES",
  "manufacturer_slug": "mennekes",
  "model": "AMTRON 4You 300 / Compact 2.0s / Start 2.0s (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "amtron-4you-300-compact-start",
  "short_model": "AMTRON 4You 300",
  "aliases": [
    "AMTRON 4You 300",
    "AMTRON 4You 310",
    "AMTRON Compact 2.0s",
    "AMTRON Start 2.0s"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "EV charger",
  "applies_to": "AMTRON 4You 300, Compact 2.0s and Start 2.0s wallboxes with software 2023.21.11024 or later (Modbus register layout v01.03).",
  "summary": "These MENNEKES home wallboxes become a Modbus RTU slave ('satellite') on RS-485 when DIP switches S1-4 and S1-5 are on, so an energy manager can control them. Data can be read as holding or input registers. This map covers identity, EVSE and CP state, configured current limits, per-phase current, voltage and power, session and lifetime energy, error codes and the control registers: heartbeat, charging release, current limit, phase switching and lock.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 50,
    "baud": 57600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed in hex and go on the wire unchanged. The specification gives no example frame, but its table starts at register 0x0000 (Modbus version), which cannot exist in 1-based numbering, so the printed numbers are protocol addresses. So 0x0302 is requested as 770 decimal."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Software 2023.21.11024 and later (Modbus register layout v01.03)",
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus RTU Specification - AMTRON 4You 300, AMTRON Compact 2.0s, AMTRON Start 2.0s",
    "doc_number": "v2.5",
    "revision_date": "2025-07-11",
    "url": "https://www.mennekes.de/fileadmin/MEN-Deutschland/emobility/01_documents/04_installer/Modbus_RTU_Specification_AMTRON_4You300_Compact_2.0s_Start_2.0s-v2.5.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 2 (bus settings, byte/word order, notes), pp. 6-7 (register table), p. 8 (EMS charging and phase-switch example)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The specification states 'Byte and Word Order: Big Endian', so float32 and uint32 values have the high word first (ABCD). Float values are in engineering units with no scaling.",
    "Each register lists the register-layout version that introduced it (v01.00-v01.03); registers added in a later layout may be missing on older firmware (0x0114, 0x0D19 and 0x001B arrived with v01.03).",
    "Charging current energy manager (0x0302): 0 means no limit and the wallbox signals its maximum (16 or 32 A); 0.01-5.99 A pauses charging; 6 A and up is a limit, clipped to the wallbox's own maximum.",
    "Error codes 2300-2305 (over/undervoltage on L1-L3, with voltage detection active) are also listed in the source alongside the codes given under values.",
    "Function codes per the source: read 0x03 or 0x04; write single register 0x06 only for 1-register values, write multiple 0x10 for floats (e.g. 0x0302)."
  ],
